{
  "dom_id": "step-45703",
  "name": "The Prefix System for Metric Units",
  "problem": "Let's recall the table that relates metric units of length.\n\n| Name | Symbol | Conversion |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Kilometer | $\\textrm{km}$ | $1\\,\\textrm{km} = 1\\,000\\,\\textrm{m}$ |\n| Meter | $\\textrm{m}$ | Base Unit |\n| Centimeter | $\\textrm{cm}$ | $100\\,\\textrm{cm} = 1\\,\\textrm{m}$ |\n| Millimeter | $\\textrm{mm}$ | $1\\,000\\,\\textrm{mm} = 1\\,\\textrm{m}$ |\n\n**Important**: Symbols in the metric system follow a consistent set of **prefix rules**, which we explain below. If you find these difficult, *do not worry*! For now, you just need to remember the conversions shown in the table above. \n\nThe prefix rules are as follows:\n\n- The prefix \"$\\textrm k$\" stands for **kilo**, which means $1\\,000$. Therefore, $1\\,\\textrm{km} = 1\\,000\\,\\textrm{m}.$\n\n- The prefix \"$\\textrm c$\" stands for **centi**, which means $\\dfrac{1}{100}$. Therefore, $1\\,\\textrm{cm} = \\dfrac{1}{100}\\,\\textrm{m}.$ \n\n Notice that if we add $1\\,\\textrm{cm}$ to itself $100$ times, we get exactly $1\\,\\textrm{m}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{100\\text{ times}}{\\overset{⏞}{1\\,\\text{cm}+1\\,\\text{cm}+⋯+1\\,\\text{cm}}} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{100}\\,\\text{m}+\\frac{1}{100}\\,\\text{m}+⋯+\\frac{1}{100}\\,\\text{m} & = \\\\ 100\\times \\frac{1}{100}\\,\\text{m} & = \\\\ \\frac{100\\times 1}{100}\\,\\text{m} & = \\\\ \\frac{100}{100}\\,\\text{m} & = \\\\ 1\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $100\\,\\textrm{cm}$ equals $1\\,\\textrm{m},$ as stated in the table.\n\n- The prefix \"$\\textrm m$\" stands for **milli**, which means $\\dfrac{1}{1\\,000}$. Therefore, $1\\,\\textrm{mm} = \\dfrac{1}{1,000}\\,\\textrm{m}.$ This means that $1\\,000\\,\\textrm{mm}$ equals $1\\,\\textrm{m},$ as shown in the table.",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-45703\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"45703\" steptype=\"tutorial\" contentid=\"7943\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-45703\" class=\"stepAnchor\" name=\"step-5\">The Prefix System for Metric Units</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"45703\">?</div>\n            </div> \n\n            <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage * {\n                            transition: none;\n                            -webkit-tran